---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | HerbGuide"
  description="Privacy information for HerbGuide, including analytics, advertising tools, and general site usage."
  robots="noindex, follow"
  structuredData={[
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "WebPage",
      name: "Privacy Policy",
      description:
        "Privacy information for HerbGuide, including analytics, advertising tools, and general site usage.",
      url: "https://herbguide.store/privacy-policy/",
    },
  ]}
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="shell narrow prose-block">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy Policy</p>
      <h1>Privacy basics</h1>
      <p>
        HerbGuide aims to keep data collection limited, explain third-party tools clearly,
        and avoid unnecessary complexity wherever possible.
      </p>
      <p>
        This page explains the main categories of information that may be collected through
        analytics, advertising, and standard website operation.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell two-up">
      <article class="prose-block card">
        <h2>What HerbGuide may collect</h2>
        <p>
          Depending on configuration, the site may use basic analytics, search console
          verification, advertising scripts, standard web server logs, and simple cookies
          related to performance or ad delivery. These tools may collect standard usage and
          device information according to their own settings and policies.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="prose-block card">
        <h2>When this policy may be updated</h2>
        <p>
          If HerbGuide adds a newsletter, contact forms, richer analytics, affiliate links,
          or additional advertising controls, this policy should be updated with more exact
          language about what data is collected, which third parties receive it, and how
          users can manage their choices.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="shell two-up">
      <article class="prose-block card">
        <h2>Analytics, search, and advertising tools</h2>
        <p>
          HerbGuide may use services such as Google Analytics, Google Search Console,
          Microsoft Bing Webmaster Tools, and Google advertising technologies to understand
          site performance, indexing, and general traffic behavior. These third-party
          services may collect standard usage information according to their own policies.
          Readers should review those providers' own privacy policies for more detail.
        </p>
        <p>
          If a reader clicks an optional support link, they are taken to a Creem checkout page.
          Payment details are handled by Creem under Creem's own policies rather than being
          processed directly on HerbGuide.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="prose-block card">
        <h2>Policy changes</h2>
        <p>
          This page may be updated to reflect changes in analytics, advertising settings,
          contact workflows, or publishing tools. The goal is to keep the policy accurate
          and reasonably easy to read.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell two-up">
      <article class="prose-block card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Site navigation</p>
        <h2>Where readers usually go after policy pages</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/about/">About HerbGuide</a></li>
          <li><a href="/safety/">Safety</a></li>
          <li><a href="/herbs/">Herb Library</a></li>
          <li><a href="/kitchen/">Kitchen Traditions</a></li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="prose-block card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Trust path</p>
        <h2>Related trust and reference pages</h2>
        <p>
          Readers who want more context about how HerbGuide works can continue to
          <a href="/about/"> About</a>, <a href="/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a>,
          and <a href="/kitchen/">Kitchen Traditions</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          If they want practical educational depth rather than policy language, a useful next
          stop is <a href="/glossary/">Glossary</a> or
          <a href="/basics/"> Basics</a>.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
